CHOWN(8)                   System Administration                    CHOWN(8)

NAME
    chown - confirm a file's owner

SYNOPSIS
    chown UID[:GID] PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Ask whether account UID owns PATH, and GID is its group if one is
    given. Both are numbers; there is no lookup by name. With no GID the
    shell reads the group back and asks for it unchanged.

    No owner is stored: stat(1) names your session's account as the
    owner of everything your session reaches. So chown stores nothing,
    and succeeds only to your own uid and group. A file is never given
    away; who may reach it is the filesystem policy's to say.

SECURITY
    The fs_server decides, through the capability your session reached
    the file by, never against who you are.

SEE ALSO
    chmod(1), stat(1)
